I've been having fun playing with the Initpoly patch recently, and I
must say that it's a lot of fun.  Most recently I played a homunculus
wizard, and this made gameplay quite unique.  Here's some things that
were different:

 * Size tiny, sleep-resistant, poison-resistant, flying
 * Can put monsters to sleep with bite
 * Too small to wear armor or wield weapons
 * Too small to open or kick-down doors (force bolt was my only way of
opening them)
 * Too small to push bolders, but could squeeze past them
 * Could not speak, so couldn't #chat with anyone

Despite limitations, he was a bit overpowered due to the sleep bite. 
The experience made me think that a pixie race would be fun to play. 
They would also be size tiny and flying, and maybe be invisible and
see invisible, then maybe later get auto-searching and telepathy. 
Give them a good amount of bonus power points as well.  Wizard would
really be the only playable class.

Anyone else discover any fun creature/class combos using this patch?


